  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Le Cabanon is a beach restaurant with a private beach, at square Roland Garros Plage, 53 boulevard de la Mer, between Port-Fréjus and the Base Nature. The sunbed booking platform MySunbed describes it on a sandy beach lined with palm trees, with a limited number of sunbeds, cooking based on fresh local produce, cocktails and a view of the Mediterranean, and gives beach hours of 9am to 5pm. This information comes from a commercial platform: no website of the restaurant's own was found.</p>
      <h2>With a dog</h2>
      <p>None of the sources consulted says whether dogs are welcome at Le Cabanon: neither the Fréjus tourist office nor a website of the restaurant. The private beach follows the operator's rules, so it's best to ask before coming whether your dog can sit at a table, on the terrace or on the beach. Don't confuse this restaurant with Le Cabanon on the Mourillon beaches in Toulon, or Le Cabanon in Cannes, which are different establishments with their own official listings.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: for a day out with your dog in Fréjus, the Pacha beach at the Base Nature is the beach reserved for dogs; you can then ask at Le Cabanon about lunch.</div>
      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Fréjus tourist office presents the Pacha beach as the town's dog beach: it is at the Base Nature, 1196 boulevard de la Mer, with free access (tourist office phone: 04 94 17 66 00). Its beaches page also mentions an area where dogs on a leash are allowed near the Argens lifeguard station. The Woof & Wow dog park (Woof Park) is listed near the restaurant. Fréjus's private beaches set their own rules.</p>
    </div>
